  "entry": "code/README.md",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A Streamlit app that turns crystal structure files into RIPER control/coord blocks and k-point paths, then parses and plots riper outputs: SCF convergence, band structures (plain and fat bands) and total or projected DOS. The app's navigation also lists pages this run did not explore: database import (Materials Project / PubChem to RIPER), structure building (Surface Builder, Place Adsorbate on Surface, Pack Molecules in Cell), RT-TDDFT and embedding input creation, spectrum plotters (LR-TDDFT UV-Vis, RT-TDDFT absorption, HHG), cube processing, and help pages (Keywords Help, Convergence Tips, Examples, References). This tree covers only the band-structure, DOS and input-preparation part of the app. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
